  "body": "Requirement [14.4.2](https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/blob/master/4.0/en/0x22-V14-Config.md#v144-http-security-headers) says:\r\n\r\n> Verify that all API responses contain a Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"api.json\" header (or other appropriate filename for the content type).\r\n\r\nIt's not clear that this actually prevents any current attack, as RFD attacks are (I believe) prevented by all modern browsers. See also [this related issue](https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-post-spectre-webdev/issues/1) on the W3C Post-Spectre web development spec.",
